# Design

Palette `{{config.design.palette}}`, radius `{{config.design.radius}}`, font `{{config.design.fontSans}}`, density `{{config.design.density}}`.

## Tokens only

Every color, radius, font, and section spacing value lives in `app/tokens.css`. Components reference those variables or the Tailwind colors mapped in `app/globals.css`.

Do not hardcode hex, rgb, hsl, or okLch values in components, pages, or modules. If a value is missing, add a token first, then use it.

`#fff`, `#ffffff`, `white`, and `black` count as hardcoded colors.

## What to use

- Page background and text: `--color-bg`, `--color-fg`
- Secondary text and surfaces: `--color-muted`, `--color-muted-fg`
- Lines: `--color-border`
- Primary action: `--color-accent`, `--color-accent-fg`
- Second color, for chips and supporting actions: `--color-highlight`, `--color-highlight-fg`
- Errors: `--color-danger`
- Corners: `--radius`
- Page padding: `--space-section`

Dark mode overrides the same variable names. Do not add a second set of one-off colors for dark mode.

## Components

{{#if flags.shadcn}}
shadcn components live in `components/ui`. Restyle them with tokens. The shadcn base color in `components.json` is only a starting point; `app/tokens.css` is the source of truth.
{{else}}
This project does not install shadcn. Style elements with the token classes in `app/globals.css`.
{{/if}}
